You can install scrcpy (along with adb) on Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) using apt—or grab the latest upstream release with pre-built scrcpy-server from GitHub.

Option 1: Install via APT (Fastest)

bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y scrcpy adb
Use code with caution.

Option 2: Install Latest Upstream Release via GitHub (Recommended for Android 14/15/16 Support)

(Using split URL strings below prevents your browser from truncating the GitHub path when you copy-paste.)
bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y adb ffmpeg libsdl2-2.0-0 libusb-1.0-0 curl tar && \
rm -rf /tmp/scrcpy_install && mkdir -p /tmp/scrcpy_install && cd /tmp/scrcpy_install && \
API_URL="https://github.com""/repos/Genymobile/scrcpy/releases/latest" && \
SCRCPY_URL=$(curl -s "$API_URL" | grep -oE 'https://[^"]+scrcpy-linux-x86_64[^"]+\.tar\.gz' | head -n 1) && \
echo "Downloading: $SCRCPY_URL" && \
wget -qO scrcpy.tar.gz "$SCRCPY_URL" && \
tar -xf scrcpy.tar.gz && \
sudo rm -rf /opt/scrcpy && \
sudo mv scrcpy-linux-x86_64-* /opt/scrcpy && \
sudo ln -sf /opt/scrcpy/scrcpy /usr/local/bin/scrcpy && \
cd ~ && rm -rf /tmp/scrcpy_install
Use code with caution.

Verify scrcpy & adb Are Installed & Ready

bash
for tool in scrcpy adb; do
  if command -v "$tool" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "✅ $tool -> $(command -v "$tool")"
  else
    echo "❌ $tool -> MISSING"
  fi
done

scrcpy --version | head -n 2
Use code with caution.
(Note: Enable USB debugging under Developer options on your Android device, plug it in via USB, accept the RSA fingerprint prompt on the phone, and run scrcpy.)
